## What this tree is

- `<Engine/>` is <the engine, source built or installed>. **Read only.** If engine behaviour needs changing, subclass it.
- `<YourProject/>` is <what it is>.
- `<YourProject>/Docs/AgentMemory/` holds the generated reflection dumps and Blueprint index. These are generated. Never hand edit them, the commandlet is the source of truth.
- `<YourProject>/Docs/Design/` holds design docs, each naming the modules and classes it governs in its front matter.

## Build commands

Call `UnrealBuildTool.exe` directly rather than `Build.bat`, because Build.bat holds a batch level lock that survives a cancelled build and blocks the next one.

```
<path to>\UnrealBuildTool.exe <YourProject>Editor Win64 Development -Project=<path>\<YourProject>.uproject
```

Regenerate the reflection dumps after any `UCLASS`, `UFUNCTION`, `UPROPERTY` or replication change:

```
<path to>\UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe <path>\<YourProject>.uproject ^
  -run=UEAgentAcceleratorTools.AgentMemoryDump -unattended -nopause -nosplash -NullRHI -Multiprocess
```

Regenerate the compile database after any `.Build.cs` or module change. All three of those flags are load bearing, and the ue-memory-stack plugin's *03-running-the-dump.md* says why.

