## Querying this codebase

Prefer a structured query over reading files. Reach for the right layer first rather than grepping by habit; most questions should never need a file read.

| Question | First stop | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| Where is X defined | `find_symbol_indexed`: clangd's whole-tree index, about 0.1s. Matching is fuzzy, so pick the exact name; `Class::Func` narrows a member. **Needs the patch in *serena/*; delete this row without it** | Grep for the file, then `find_symbol` with `relative_path` |
| What does X derive from, the **full** chain | `Docs/AgentMemory/classes/<Class>.md`, the `Inherits:` line, which carries the whole chain to `UObject` | `index.md` gives the **immediate** parent only, so chasing a chain through it costs one grep per level |
| Who calls X, blast radius of a change | `find_referencing_symbols` for C++, **and the Blueprint half**: read `Docs/AgentMemory/bpcallers/<OwningClass>.md`. Both, always | ripgrep, C++ only |
| Which Blueprints derive from X, implement Y, are data only | grep `Docs/AgentMemory/Blueprints.md` for the native parent, then read `blueprints/<Parent>.md` | none |
| What does X's comment say | `find_symbol(include_info=True)` | read the file |
| Is X BlueprintCallable, replicated, under which `COND_` | grep `Docs/AgentMemory/index.md` for the class, then read `classes/<Class>.md`. **Check its size first and grep it instead if it is over ~5 KB.** Never read the index whole | never clangd, it cannot see any of this |
| Why is this system built this way | `<YourProject>/Docs/Design/*.md` | source history |
| TODO, HACK, inline notes | `search_for_pattern` if your Serena context exposes it (the stock `claude-code` one does not), otherwise Grep | none, text search is the only route |
| C# build system, `.Build.cs`, UBT | <Serena with a C# language server> | ripgrep |
| Build commands, module map, conventions | already in this file | none needed |

**Important: never call `find_symbol` without `relative_path`.** It walks every file in every workspace folder instead of using the index. With the engine in the workspace it times out, and the walk carries on after the timeout until it crashes clangd. The scope guard in *serena/* refuses the call, and refuses directories over 1,000 source files. Scoped to a header it takes 0.01–12s. Get the file from `find_symbol_indexed` first. Check its location once: an out-of-line method resolves to its `.cpp`, and a `UENUM` can resolve to its `.generated.h` under `Intermediate/`.

**`find_symbol_indexed` returns `[]` straight after a server restart**, in about 0.1s, until clangd has opened a file. That empty answer doesn't mean "no such symbol". Make one scoped call first and ask again.

**Important:** a caller list is not complete until you have read the Blueprint half as well. A Blueprint graph calling a `BlueprintCallable` function is a caller no C++ tool can see, `rg` skips `.uasset` silently, and renaming the function still compiles. Those files are generated from resolved graph nodes and cover calls, property reads and property writes, so **a class absent from the index genuinely has no Blueprint users**. Never answer a blast radius question from C++ alone, and never fall back to `strings` on a `.uasset`: the index is the answer and the binary is not.

**Important:** a per-class artefact is usually small and occasionally is not, so **check the size before reading one whole**. The median is around 1 KB, but the biggest class in a large module can be 30 KB or more. Grep the file for the row you want, or read the Properties or Functions table alone.

**Important:** for anything about units, ranges, bounds or contracts, the comment alone is not an answer. Read the body as well. Hover returns the comment with nothing to contradict it, so on this class of question the cheap route is the accurate one.

Escalate cheapest first: this file (free), the reflection dump, a symbol query, hover, then whole files. That last one is where we started before any of this existed.

