## Conventions that get got wrong unaided

<Keep the ones that apply, delete the rest, add your own. These are the ones that come up on any UE project.>

- `GENERATED_BODY()` goes immediately after the opening brace of a `UCLASS` or `USTRUCT`, and the file includes `<ClassName>.generated.h` **last**. Adding a line above `GENERATED_BODY()` invalidates the generated header until the next build, because it keys off `__LINE__`.
- Reflection macros are parsed by UnrealHeaderTool, not the C preprocessor, so clangd sees none of them. The reflection dump is the authority on specifiers and replication.
- A `UPROPERTY(Replicated)` does nothing on its own. It needs an entry in `GetLifetimeReplicatedProps`, and the `COND_` lives there rather than in the header.
- A `UFUNCTION` on an interface must be redeclared in every implementing class. For a plain virtual that Blueprints and the reflection system never see, leave the `UFUNCTION` off entirely.
- Prefer `TObjectPtr<T>` over raw pointers for `UPROPERTY` members.
